{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"1b1f945f7a46e377d1b461a21d00dbd8cc55e5dd54391ea8e943b3e7d2dfb1fd","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM structured output parser","key_entities":["rebar.llm.structured","_candidate_dicts","_select_and_validate","_all_json_objects","parse_structured","tests/unit/test_structured.py","tests/unit/test_pai_output.py","src/rebar/llm/structured.py:483-499","src/rebar/llm/structured.py:547-558"],"problem_keywords":["structured output","duplicate candidates","false ambiguity warning","JSON parsing","candidate deduplication"],"propositions":["Ordinary structured replies with a single JSON object emit false 'multiple candidates validated' warnings despite semantic identity.","The parser duplicates a single decoded JSON object by appending it twice—once from _all_json_objects() and once from json.loads().","Identity checks on separately constructed Pydantic instances incorrectly trigger ambiguity warnings when the objects are semantically equal.","Deduplicating semantically identical decoded candidates in discovery order before validation eliminates false warnings while preserving last-valid-wins for genuinely distinct candidates.","Focused test suite (structured.py, pai_output.py, review_kernel.py, completion_verifier.py) validates candidate selection, warning behavior, and parser integrity post-fix."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787770835675145001,"uuid":"2b30cd79-04f3-4f6b-a186-20fdfadbf0a7"}